course: dictionary
lesson: 6800
title: One word, many meanings: organ
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word is the same, but the meaning changes with the sentence around it. The context tells you which meaning is right. Look at the words around the word first.
explain: «Your brain is a soft, wrinkly organ» tells you organ is a part of the body with a special job. But «The church organ filled the hall with sound» is about a big musical instrument with pipes and keys. The clues are church, sound and hall.
explain: Plants have organs too. A leaf or a root is a plant organ, because it has a special job for the plant. Ask yourself: what is the sentence about? Then try the meaning in the sentence to see if it fits.
fact: Organ can mean a part of the body with a special job, such as the heart, lungs, brain, stomach or skin.
fact: Organ can mean a large musical instrument with pipes and keyboards, played in churches and concert halls.
fact: Organ can also mean a part of a plant with a special job, such as a leaf or a root.
fact: «Vital organs» are organs your body cannot live without, such as the heart and the brain.
fact: «The brain is about 1.4 kilograms in an adult» and is made of about 86 billion nerve cells.
exercise: «Your heart is an organ that pumps blood around your body.» What is an organ in this sentence? | A large musical instrument | *A part of the body with a special job | A type of stone | A kind of bird
exercise: «The church organ filled the hall with sound.» What does organ mean here? | *A large musical instrument with pipes and keys | A type of bone | A leaf on a plant | A part of the body
exercise: Which of these is a plant organ, not a part of the body? | Stomach | Skin | Heart | *Root
test: «Blood tests can check how organs are working.» What does organ mean here? | A plant's leaf | *A part of the body with a special job | A large musical instrument with pipes | A kind of shell
test: Ella will play the organ at the concert in the big hall. What is an organ in this sentence? | A part of the body that pumps blood | A type of bone in the hips | *A large musical instrument with pipes and keyboards | A part of a plant
exam: «Ollie hears that the organ must match the sick person's body.» What does organ mean here? | A large musical instrument with pipes | A part of a plant | *A part of the body with a special job | A shape made of bones
